	<logo>https://static.globalissues.org/i/globalissues/logo-feed.jpg</logo><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44603</id><title>New Working Group Seeks Justice for Critical Mineral Mining Communities</title><updated>2026-11-16T10:32:49-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44603" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/Dr-Augustine-Njamnshi-of-ACSEA.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/Dr-Augustine-Njamnshi-of-ACSEA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/Dr-Augustine-Njamnshi-of-ACSEA-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/Dr-Augustine-Njamnshi-of-ACSEA.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
ANTALYA, Türkiye, November 16 (IPS)  - A coalition of African civil society organisations, representatives from the Africa Institute of Resilience Studies (an independent organisation working in research, policy, training and capacity development),&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;and representatives from the Bank–Civil Society Coalition, which brings together seven major regional networks and civil society organisations working on climate and energy, have launched the African Non-State Actors Working Group on Critical Minerals on the sidelines of COP 31 in Antalya, Türkiye.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44603&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “New Working Group Seeks Justice for Critical Mineral Mining Communities”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44602</id><title>The Legal Path to Autocracy</title><updated>2026-11-16T09:39:37-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44602" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/UK-based-Zimbabweans_.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/UK-based-Zimbabweans_.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/UK-based-Zimbabweans_-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/UK-based-Zimbabweans_.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
MONTEVIDEO, Uruguay, November 16 (IPS)  - Zimbabwe’s President Emmerson Mnangagwa, who took over when a miliary coup ended Robert Mugabe’s 37 years in power, has made clear he has no intention of limiting himself to a decade at the top. In July, he signed a &lt;a href=&quot;https://liberties.aljazeera.com/en/zimbabwe-extends-mnangagwas-rule-by-constitutional-amendment/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;constitutional amendment&lt;/a&gt; that lengthened the terms of the sitting president and parliament from five to seven years and pushed the next general election back from 2028 to 2030.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44602&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “The Legal Path to Autocracy”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44601</id><title>Africa Makes Some Gains but Faces Major Setbacks at COP31</title><updated>2026-11-16T08:28:52-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44601" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/Activists-protesting-against-use-of-fossil-fuels-at-COP31-in-Antalya-Turkey.-Credit-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe-1.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/Activists-protesting-against-use-of-fossil-fuels-at-COP31-in-Antalya-Turkey.-Credit-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/Activists-protesting-against-use-of-fossil-fuels-at-COP31-in-Antalya-Turkey.-Credit-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe-1-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/Activists-protesting-against-use-of-fossil-fuels-at-COP31-in-Antalya-Turkey.-Credit-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe-1.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
ANTALYA, Türkiye, November 16 (IPS)  - Today (November 15) marks the second week of negotiations at the United Nations climate summit in the resort city of Antalya, Turkey.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44601&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Africa Makes Some Gains but Faces Major Setbacks at COP31”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44599</id><title>Time to Home</title><updated>2026-11-16T05:59:24-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44599" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/11/Amy-Pope-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;
UNITED NATIONS, November 16 (IPS)  - Somewhere tonight, a family that lost its home to the water is asleep in a school gymnasium. The tent, the blankets and the first meal arrived within hours. But a secure home will take years. Every climate disaster ends with the same question, and few climate budgets have a line for it: where will we sleep tonight?
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44599&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Time to Home”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44607</id><title>Funding cuts raise risks of trafficking and exploitation for refugee children</title><updated>2026-11-16T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44607" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/28-02-2023-UNICEF-Bangladesh.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/28-02-2023-UNICEF-Bangladesh.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/28-02-2023-UNICEF-Bangladesh.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/28-02-2023-UNICEF-Bangladesh.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sharp reductions in humanitarian funding are putting refugees, particularly children, at increased risk of being trafficked, exploited or abused, while the systems that protect them are weakening. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44607&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Funding cuts raise risks of trafficking and exploitation for refugee children”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44606</id><title>Guterres calls for a legally binding instrument for ‘killer robots'</title><updated>2026-11-16T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44606" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/23-10-2026-UN-Abyei-Sudan-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/23-10-2026-UN-Abyei-Sudan-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/23-10-2026-UN-Abyei-Sudan-01.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/23-10-2026-UN-Abyei-Sudan-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Talks began in Geneva on Monday to push for controls on lethal autonomous weapons systems that are often referred to as “killer robots”.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44606&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Guterres calls for a legally binding instrument for ‘killer robots&#039;”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44605</id><title>At his final ASEAN-UN Summit, Guterres upholds cooperation and action on Myanmar</title><updated>2026-11-16T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44605" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/15-11-2026_SG-ASEANSummit.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/15-11-2026_SG-ASEANSummit.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/15-11-2026_SG-ASEANSummit.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/15-11-2026_SG-ASEANSummit.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;UN Secretary-General António Guterres underscored the need for stronger collaboration with the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) and an end to the crisis in Myanmar, in remarks to regional leaders meeting in the Philippine capital Manila on Monday. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/16/44605&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “At his final ASEAN-UN Summit, Guterres upholds cooperation and action on Myanmar”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/15/44604</id><title>First Person: Managing risk on Ukraine’s frontline</title><updated>2026-11-15T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/15/44604" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/10-01-2025-UNOCHA-Ukraine-03.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/10-01-2025-UNOCHA-Ukraine-03.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/10-01-2025-UNOCHA-Ukraine-03.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/10-01-2025-UNOCHA-Ukraine-03.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Humanitarian workers providing support to communities on the frontline of the war between Ukraine and Russia must balance remaining close to those in need with the heightened risks of operating in a conflict zone, according to the top UN official in Ukraine.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/15/44604&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “First Person: Managing risk on Ukraine’s frontline”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/15/44600</id><title>Empowering faith and Indigenous leaders to combat hate</title><updated>2026-11-15T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/15/44600" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/15-11-2026-traditional-leaders.JPG/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/15-11-2026-traditional-leaders.JPG/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/15-11-2026-traditional-leaders.JPG/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/15-11-2026-traditional-leaders.JPG/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Religious, traditional and Indigenous leaders need to be empowered to act as full partners in preventing conflict, not just praised for their role, speakers said Sunday at the opening of the Muscat Plan of Action Forum in Oman.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/15/44600&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Empowering faith and Indigenous leaders to combat hate”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/15/44598</id><title>Nadia Murad: ‘Day by day, I took my story back’</title><updated>2026-11-15T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/15/44598" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/12-11-2026_UN-Publications_Murad.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/12-11-2026_UN-Publications_Murad.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/12-11-2026_UN-Publications_Murad.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/11/12-11-2026_UN-Publications_Murad.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Nobel Peace Prize laureate Nadia Murad has spent years telling the world about the atrocities committed against her and the Yazidi community by militants from the terrorist group, ISIL. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/11/15/44598&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Nadia Murad: ‘Day by day, I took my story back’”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry></feed><!-- 0.0042s ch:0 -->